  ei_name: "Albert Einstein", ei_zeit: "1879–1955", ei_kurz: "How long does light take to reach us from the Sun?",
  ei_story: "As a teenager Einstein wondered what the world would look like if he could ride on a beam of light. In 1905 he published the theory of relativity: nothing is faster than light – it travels about 300,000 km every second. His theory also leads to the famous formula E = m · c². Because light needs time, we always see the Sun as it looked a little over 8 minutes ago.",
