  n_name: "Isaac Newton", n_zeit: "1643–1727", n_kurz: "How heavy are you on the Moon?",
  n_story: "Legend has it that Newton saw an apple fall from a tree and wondered: why does it fall down – and why doesn’t the Moon fall onto the Earth too? He realised that the same force does both: gravity. On the Moon it is much weaker than on Earth, on Jupiter much stronger. Your mass stays the same everywhere – only the force pulling you down changes.",
